Shared Jetson measurement harness (owner: jetson-harness track)
================================================================
Installed at ~/synthlab/harness/. Source: repo branch jetson-harness, synthlab/harness/.
Do not edit files here; ask the jetson-harness track. Write outputs under YOUR folder.

EVERY timed run must hold the shared lock (from the Mac):
  tools/jetson.sh measured '<command>'
Keep one locked command under ~20 minutes.

THERMAL
  python3 ~/synthlab/harness/run_thermal_bank.py \
      --bank ~/synthlab/<track>/banks/<bank> --out ~/synthlab/<track>/runs/<new_dir> \
      [--seconds 60] [--warmup 15] [--fps 8.7] [--unpaced] \
      [--backend pytorch|tensorrt|none] [--repeats N]
  bank   : frames.npy uint16 (N,120,160) TLinear counts (0.01 K/count) + manifest.json
  does   : TLinear->Celsius, fixed 10..50 C -> 8-bit, block image entropy (HT), YOLOv8n
           (pytorch = CUDA FP32, as in the original project; tensorrt = FP16 engine), NMS
  writes : frames.csv   one row per frame: convert_ms, bie_ms, prep_ms, yolo_pre_ms,
                        yolo_inf_ms, yolo_post_ms (NMS), yolo_wall_ms, yolo_extract_ms,
                        total_ms, HT, n_det, n_person, n_candidates (pre-NMS), max_conf
           tegrastats.csv   timestamped raw tegrastats lines every 200 ms
           summary.json     means, p50/p95/p99, power_w, energy_per_frame_j, idle power,
                            telemetry coverage checks ("ok": true/false, "problems": [...])
  modes  : paced (default) = one frame every 1/8.7 s like the Lepton; --unpaced = as fast
           as possible (GPU busy all the time, so power differences are easier to see)
  quick check (about 25 s):  --seconds 10 --warmup 5

LIDAR
  python3 ~/synthlab/harness/run_lidar_bank.py \
      --bank ~/synthlab/<track>/banks/<bank> --out ~/synthlab/<track>/runs/<new_dir> \
      [--window 1.0] [--workload entropy|cluster|both] [--seconds 60] [--warmup 10] \
      [--unpaced] [--z-min -0.85] [--roi -6 6 -6 6 -2 3] [--repeats N]
  bank   : frame_00000.npz ... (100 ms frames; xyz float32 (M,3) sensor frame, tag uint8)
           + manifest.json. 10 frames make one 1 s window; leftover frames are unused.
  does   : entropy = ROI crop -> 5 cm voxel downsample -> radius 0.20 m kNN (k_max 150,
           k_min 10, scipy cKDTree) -> covariance eigenvalues -> L,P,S -> H_DS, H_eigen
           cluster = Euclidean clustering (0.10 m) + person-candidate size filter
  writes : windows.csv  one row per window: accumulate_ms, roi_ms, voxel_ms, knn_ms,
                        eig_ms, entropy_ms, cl_pairs_ms, cl_cc_ms, cl_stats_ms,
                        entropy_total_ms, cluster_total_ms, total_ms, H_DS, H_eigen,
                        mean_L/P/S, frac_high_S, n_raw, n_roi, n_voxel, n_pairs,
                        n_clusters, n_person_candidates, frac_tag_particle
           tegrastats.csv, summary.json (as above, energy_per_window_j)
  notes  : --z-min is the floor cut in the SENSOR frame (default -0.85 m is the LiDAR
           track's value); set it for your sensor height. Cost grows fast with the number
           of occupied 5 cm voxels: ~100k voxels takes ~2.8 s per window on this Jetson,
           so a 1 s paced window overruns (summary.json reports overrun_windows).

SELF-TEST BANKS (made-up, not research data): ~/synthlab/harness/selftest_banks/
  thermal_flat, thermal_blobs, lidar_room, lidar_room_fog

Not measured: camera/LiDAR acquisition, USB/network transfer, disk reads (banks are looped
from RAM). Power is tegrastats VDD_IN (module input), not wall power.
